{"title":"Naming AI models correctly","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/913157858/0/marginalrevolution~Naming-AI-models-correctly.html","date":1739778677000,"content":"<p>Are you confused by all the model names and terminology running around?  Here is a simple guide to <em>what I call them</em>:</p>\r\n<p>o1 pro — The Boss</p>\r\n<p>4o — Little Boss</p>\r\n<p>o3 mini — The Mini Boss</p>\r\n<p>GPT 4o with scheduled tasks — Boss come back later</p>\r\n<p>o1 — Cheapskates’ boss</p>\r\n<p>Deep Research — My research assistant</p>\r\n<p>GPT-4 — Former Boss</p>\r\n<p>DeepSeek — China Boss</p>\r\n<p>Claude — Claude</p>\r\n<p>Llama 3.3, or whichever — Meta.  I never quite got used to calling Facebook “Meta,” so I call the AI model Meta too.  Hope that’s OK!</p>\r\n<p>Grok 3 — Elon</p>\r\n<p>Gemini 2.0 Flash — China Boss suggests “Laggy Larry,” but I don’t actually call it that.</p>\r\n<p>Perplexity.ai — Google</p>\r\n<p>Got that?  Easy as pie!</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/02/naming-ai-models-correctly.html\">Naming AI models correctly</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/913157858/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/913157858/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/913157858/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/913157858/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/19/913157858/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.